  "memo": "Adobe Inc. (ADBE) delivered another strong year in FY2024, capping off a multi-year run of robust growth driven by its dominant Creative Cloud and Document Cloud franchises. Revenue reached $21.2 billion, up 11% year-over-year, marking the 10th consecutive year of double-digit growth. Operating income grew 14% to $7.8 billion, while net income rose 12% to $5.9 billion, translating to diluted EPS of $12.75, a 13% increase. Free cash flow remained robust at $7.1 billion, underpinning the company’s ability to return capital to shareholders via dividends and buybacks. Gross margins expanded to 88%, reflecting the high-margin nature of its subscription-based model, while operating margins improved to 37%. Over the past three years, Adobe has consistently grown revenue at a 12-14% CAGR, with digital media (60% of revenue) and digital experience (30%) segments both contributing meaningfully. The acquisition of Figma in 2022 has begun to integrate well, though synergies are still ramping. Looking ahead, AI-driven features across its Creative Suite and Experience Cloud are expected to be key growth drivers. Valuation remains rich at ~35x forward earnings, but the company’s secular growth and cash generation justify a premium. Hold for now, with a positive bias on long-term fundamentals."
}
